<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Overnight rates next month are likely to be tight, in the double digit range, with a net outflow in excess of 30,000 million rupees inspite of accommodating a lower advance tax outflow.</p>
<p>However, majority of the outflows are likely to occur in the latter half of December and the first fortnight should be easier. Reserve Bank's operations in the foreign exchange markets need to be watched carefully, particularly with US$ 2.2 billion of India Development Bonds due for redemption in mid January and mid February.</p>
<p>If RBI buys the greenback actively in the spot market, the rupees released into the system could dilute the impact of 30,000 million outflow fo a certain extent.</p>
